# Repository research instructions

Follow [`../AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md). Before any mathematical work, read
[`../docs/STATE.md`](../docs/STATE.md).

Level I remains open. Target A and Target B remain open; Target C has C-I closed and
C-II open.

Key rules:

- `docs/STATE.md` and `docs/state/theorem-state.yaml` control lifecycle/status;
- active target route maps and the modules they explicitly name control theorem content;
- reports are `unreviewed` by default; historical prompts, archive snapshots, merged PRs, and computations are not canonical unless explicitly promoted;
- Target A currently runs through Section 177; Section 175's interior-tube right-deficiency inequality is the preferred locked-branch endpoint, Sections 176–177 add zero-slack, edge-lens/coarse-Hall, and source-gate refinements, and both global conversion steps remain open;
- Target B's exact sufficient closure is `G+E >= (sqrt(3)/4) B + (sqrt(3)/2)(t+chi-1)`; the independently audited dense-grid/penetration/interpolation tools are canonical under their stated scopes, but the multi-grain shell-stability endpoint remains open;
- Target C has C-I closed and C-II open; use `docs/targets/target-c/CURRENT.md` for its full-core face-coupled finite-move and separate macroscopic-container obligations. Audit.230's quarter-fold population result does not supply an integrated endpoint or moved-geometry capacity;
- preserve the exact global-minimizer quantifiers;
- do not silently identify the genuine source with an independently constructed
  optimum, scaffold, response network, or selected stress;
- check named regressions/corrections before importing an older report;
- a frontier-changing promotion must increment `state_version`, update the state lock, machine manifest, affected route/current-frontier file and active prompt, and regenerate/verify the artifact index and state views in the same change;
- run `python3 tools/check_theorem_state_pr.py` for repository-state checks; pull-request transaction checks use `python3 tools/check_theorem_state_pr.py --base-ref <base>`.

If any operational document disagrees with `docs/STATE.md` on lifecycle/status, the
state lock controls and the disagreement itself is a repository bug to fix.

Permanent governance: mathematical proof reviews and promotions are AI-agent-only.
One independent reviewer AI session may be operated by the project owner to audit
other agents' work and must check both the complete proof and its decisive bridge
and regressions. No human referee or second agent audit is required. See
`docs/REVIEW_POLICY.md`.
